.TH MOUSE-SCROLL-TOGGLE 1 2026-11-25 "mouse-scroll-toggle" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mouse-scroll-toggle \- toggle KDE middle-button (drag) scrolling
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mouse-scroll-toggle
.RI [ on | off | toggle | status ]
.RB [ \-\-device
.IR NAME ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mouse-scroll-toggle
flips the KDE setting
.RB \(lq "Scroll when moving the pointer while pressing the middle button" \(rq
(libinput
.IR scroll\-on\-button\-down )
for pointer devices.
.P
With the feature on, holding the middle button turns pointer motion into
scrolling, which means the middle button is swallowed and never reaches
applications \(em typically breaking middle-click actions in games. Turning it
off restores a normal middle click.
.P
Changes are applied live through
.BR org.kde.KWin
and persisted to
.IR ~/.config/kcminputrc
by KWin itself; the new state survives logout and reboot. A desktop
notification is shown when the state changes.
.P
When turning the feature on, the script re-enables only the devices it last
switched off, so unrelated devices that happen to support the feature are left
alone. Without such a record it falls back to every matching device.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B on
Enable middle-button scrolling.
.TP
.B off
Disable middle-button scrolling.
.TP
.B toggle
Flip the current state. This is the default.
.TP
.B status
Print each matching device and its current state, then exit.
.TP
.BI \-\-device " NAME"
Only act on devices whose name contains
.IR NAME .
By default every pointer device that supports the feature is considered.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/kcminputrc
Per-device libinput settings written by KWin, including
.IR ScrollMethod .
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/mouse-scroll-toggle/devices
Sysnames of the devices most recently switched off, used to restore exactly
those devices when turning the feature back on.
.SH EXAMPLES
Enable or disable the feature ahead of a game:
.EX
mouse-scroll-toggle off
mouse-scroll-toggle on
.EE
.P
Bind
.B toggle
to a global shortcut (for example
.IR Meta+Shift+M )
by putting it in the
.I Exec=
line of a
.I .desktop
file marked
.IR X\-KDE\-GlobalAccel\-CommandShortcut=true .
.P
Restrict to one device:
.EX
mouse-scroll-toggle status --device "CX 2.4G"
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR kwin_wayland (1),
.BR busctl (1),
.BR kwriteconfig6 (1)
